4.1 qa/tools/gen_rain_ripple.py (3018 bytes) - GENERATOR, no verification mode

  Purpose (docstring :1-10): generates Astra's own rain-ripple flipbook, "no borrowed
  artwork". Model: a field of expanding circular wavelets; the summed height field is
  differentiated into a normal map; life shorter than the sheet and centres wrap, so the
  animation loops seamlessly in both time and space. Three sheets differ in wavelet count,
  expansion rate and ring width so the shader can stack them by rain intensity.

  Key lines:
    :14        S = 128; F = 60          (128x128 tiles, 60 frames -> 128x7680 sheet)
    :18-43     def make_sheet(n_wavelets, speed, ring_w, amp, life_frac, seed)
    :19        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)   <- numpy PCG64, NOT java.util.Random
    :36-38     periodic distance (dx = min(dx, S-dx)) -> tiles in space
    :45-57     def to_normal(frames, slope): np.gradient -> encoded RGBA normal map
    :60-63     specs = the three sheets, seeds 101 / 202 / 303
    :69-70     path = f"Astra/shaders/textures/{name}"; Image.fromarray(tall,"RGBA").save(path)
